invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont.c
catches: rsa_ifma_model_test
reason: power_of_two_mod starts rem at bit 0 of its top word whatever the
  exponent, so rsa_vp1_cpu hands rsa_ifma_public 2^(104n - e) mod m,
  where e is the exponent mod 64. At RSA-2048 e is 0 and the bytes are
  the same. At RSA-3072 e is 32, and bin/rsa_ifma_model_test, which
  compiles rsa_mont.c's dispatch over the lane model at every word count
  from 32 to 64, finds rsa_vp1_cpu under the bit giving other bytes than
  rsa_vp1 there, on any machine.

--- old
    rem[k - 1] = (uint64_t)1 << (exponent & 63);
--- new
    rem[k - 1] = 1;
